West Lancashire Borough Council proposes to undertake a Sustainable Organisation Review, the purpose of which is to reappraise fundamentally the Council&#039;s operating model, and to identify opportunities for further income generation and efficiencies across all services - General Services (GRA) and our Council Housing stock (HRA) - with the aim of ensuring that the Council can deliver its vision, key priorities, and maintain service provision and financial sustainability beyond 2020/21.which would involve a study or studies and associated work, and which would consider:
(i)	How the Council&#039;s activities are currently organised and configured, its fitness for future purpose, and whether there is scope for further efficiencies and savings, that minimise the impact on front line service delivery;
(ii)	The scope to generate additional income to be able to continue to fund existing services or to develop new services;
(iii)	Good practice examples from other public sector organisations;
and provide:
(iv)	Options and recommendations in relation to income generation and efficiency, e.g. different ways of configuring services, the future officer/staffing structure, and opportunities for a flatter structure and different organisational models.
The Council requires experienced and suitably qualified consultants to undertake key aspects of the Review.  The consultancy activity is divided into two Lots: 
Lot 1 Organisation Review, including an organisational staffing and culture review, income generation and ICT advice. 
Lot 2: Optional Additional Services, primarily specialised support in order to achieve the outcomes resulting from the Organisation Review.

West Lancashire Borough Council proposes to undertake a Sustainable Organisation Review (&#039;Review&#039;), the purpose of which will be to reappraise fundamentally the Council&#039;s operating model, and to identify opportunities for further income generation and efficiencies across all services.  The aim of the Review is to ensure that the Council can deliver its vision (&#039;To be a Council which is ambitious for West Lancashire - our Economy, Environment and for Health and Wellbeing&#039;), key priorities, and maintain service provision and financial sustainability beyond 2020/21.
It is anticipated that the Council will appoint experienced and suitably qualified consultants to undertake key aspects of the Review, for which a tendering exercise or exercises will be necessary.
Prior to embarking on a tendering exercise, the Council is launching a Soft Market Testing exercise, with the following objectives: 
(1) to facilitate early engagement with the market to ensure that the widest possible range of interested organisations are fully aware of the project, its scope and timescales;
(2) to allow interested organisations with appropriate experience to outline their views and provide information with no commitment to themselves or to the Council; 
(3) to allow the Council to confirm, or encourage critical assessment of, the viability of its plans;
(4) to gain expert input to inform the specifications for the tender exercise, and the structure and phasing of the tender requirements, in order to make the most of the opportunities, expertise and options available.
We emphasise that this is a soft market testing exercise, NOT a call for competition. 
A questionnaire, together with further details of the project and programme, and the Council&#039;s key priorities, can be downloaded from The Chest portal at www.the-chest.org.uk 
